        about_vsync: "Waits for the screen before showing a frame, so none of them is torn in two.",
        about_frame_limit: "The most frames that are drawn a second. The fight runs at {ticks} ticks a second, so that is as low as it goes.",
        about_performance: "# Minimal\nRenders just the framerate as well as CPU & GPU frametimes.\n\n# Full\nShows all tracked/labelled objects the engine is working on in a scene currently.",
        about_gui_scale: "How big the menus and the HUD are drawn, on top of fitting the window.",
        about_ui_skin: "The skin used to render the menus and the HUD.",
        about_ui_theme: "The rendered theme of the UI skin, **not all skins have multiple themes.**",
        about_transitions: "How one screen hands over to the next. Mixed melts the menus into each other and rots a fight in and out.",
        about_crt: "Draws the game like it is on a crusty old picture tube, the way god intended pixel art to be shown.",
        about_bloom: "A soft glow around light emitters like the lanterns and whatever else shines in a fight.",
        about_pathtraced: "Path tracing calculates multiple summed irradiance passes over the scenes light emitters, the result is that light bounces off the arena and its sprites. Wants a proper GPU.",
        about_light_quality: "How finely the pathtraced light is worked out. Low costs about half of High, the light around smaller lamps shimmer a touch more.\n\nMedium looks perfect, high _is_ pixel perfect.",
        about_camera_zoom: "How zoomed in the camera is during a fight. Closer is bigger fighters, further out is more of the arena.",
        about_input_display: "Shows both players inputs as a waterfall down the sides of the HUD.",
        about_hit_callouts: "Calls out what every attack resolved to. HIT, COUNTER HIT, PUNISH, BLOCKED, PARRY or WHIFF.",
        about_frame_data: "Adds the startup of a move to the callouts, and who gets to act first after it. For the lab rats, Jean.",
        about_hitboxes: "Draws all the active collision boxes over all colliders in a scene.",
